WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:07.760
Today in America there is $1.7
trillion of student debts.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.860
People should have access
to quality education

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.980
for a reasonable amount of money.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.740
This is the case in
all European countries.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.320
This is the case in many Asian countries.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.693
The case in like most countries actually.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.830
You know sometimes most ideas

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.070
are ideas searching for a problem

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.663
and we're a problem searching
for decades for a solution.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.473
Our goal, the mission
of Mos is to tear down

00:00:39.473 --> 00:00:43.023
all financial barriers to
opportunity to everyone.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.903
I'm Amira Yahyaoui and
I'm the founder of Mos.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:57.360
I was born and raised in
Tunisia, grew up in Tunisia

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.730
under a dictatorship at that time.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.756
I was very active when I was young,

00:01:02.756 --> 00:01:06.123
against the dictatorship and
was part of the Arab Spring.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.070
I was one of those who started

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:15.210
these social movements
online, as a blogger.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:19.110
I was on Twitter talking
about human rights abuses

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:19.943
in my country.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:21.923
At the time

00:01:21.923 --> 00:01:26.370
I was definitely one of the
youngest activists out there.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:30.840
So one day I was kidnapped in the street

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.610
and threw out of the borders
and made my way to Europe.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.320
So I lived in France.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.520
I worked illegally for
all sort of underpaid jobs

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.950
like dog sittings, babysitting,

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.513
anything sitting basically.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.620
In 2011, Tunisia became a democracy

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.560
and I felt like my job was done.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.570
What I owe my country was done,

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:01.588
and that's how I decided to
jump into my next chapter.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.990
I moved to the US in 2018.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.123
So when I came here to San Francisco,

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.790
I was like spending

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:15.090
a lot of time with Uber
drivers talking to them

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.830
and to their families to understand

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.370
if you can fix anything in
the world, what would you fix?

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.490
For them it was how can I make sure

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:27.510
that my children have a
better future than mine?

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.810
And this is where it was so
interesting to go dig deep

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.400
into what does that mean?

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.503
And that's how actually Mos started.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.238
Mos is a financial app

00:02:40.238 --> 00:02:44.051
that helps you tear down
financial barriers to opportunity.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.440
The idea of Mos

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.870
is how do you take those
financial solutions

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.400
that are built for the 1%

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.470
and make them accessible to the 99%?

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:54.090
What is incredible in this country

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:58.440
is that the cost of college
is like flight tickets.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.830
You can be sitting here paying $200

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.780
the person next to you is paying 1,000

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.690
and next person next
to you is paying zero.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:11.400
And so Mos' job is to make you
the person who's paying zero.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:17.070
Mos has a set of financial
features that helps you

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.710
with the biggest financial
problems you will face

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:20.850
in your first years of adulting.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:23.040
And we attack the problem

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.130
of college tuition through two ways.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:30.870
One, by making colleges
asking you for less.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.600
And two, by getting you
the maximum of free money

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.653
you are eligible for.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.930
One of the most incredible things we do

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.770
is that Mos has the biggest
scholarship pool in America.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.598
We have over $160
billion of financial aid.

00:03:46.598 --> 00:03:49.470
And this is the place for scholarship.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.940
We have like a ton of scholarship

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:54.330
but what is good is why
I opened my Mos account.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.270
They know, for example,
that Mos knows already

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.630
that I'm a Hispanic student
and that I come from Texas.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.520
So, instead of me being lost

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.390
into the $160 billion of scholarship

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.970
that Mos has for everybody,

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.760
I have the ones that I
know will be good for me.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.830
I have the high chance Texas grants.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:14.730
They're all here.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.897
Some like $10,000, $3,000,

00:04:17.897 --> 00:04:22.380
$3,000, $10,000 and I
can just go and apply.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.570
The other thing that we have at Mos

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.420
is that we actually give you cash back

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.223
on applying for scholarships.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:33.000
We actually help you get money

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.870
by getting you jobs
through our gigs platform.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.780
So we work with gig partners

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.190
who are looking for students

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.133
and pay students well and
we connect you with those.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.450
People think it's crazy

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.180
that the financial app
gives you free money

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.460
or a bank gives you free money.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:56.403
We're very different from what's in there.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.070
I am absolutely amazed by
the work that has been done

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.150
by all the activists who
are fighting every day

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.490
to get people a fair future,

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.430
a better education, access to education.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:14.940
I believe that the ultimate goal

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.790
is that we do not let people

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.680
borrow insane amount of monies

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.043
and then beg for a savior

00:05:22.043 --> 00:05:25.500
to come and give that money to them back.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.970
Nearly 45%

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.703
can have their student
debt fully canceled.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.700
That's 20 million people

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.863
who can start getting on with their lives.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:43.390
There is a true business
potential in the 99%

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:50.240
and making them better,
making them earn more.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:53.040
By earning more, they will spend more.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:57.030
By earning more, they
will enjoy life more.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:00.720
By earning more, they
will enjoy the solution

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.340
you gave them more.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.930
And so if you think about it

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.700
just from a business perspective,

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.010
that is already like a win-win.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.140
I'm absurdly optimistic.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.170
I really do believe things can change.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:16.080
I believe that the future can be bright.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.410
I'm someone that wakes
up happy in the morning.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:25.410
And so I always think
about the biggest problems

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.133
in a positive mindset
and that keeps me going.

